+# Final report — 2026-10-10-glm-prefill-250-vllm
+
+**Objective:** Port the weight-stationary prefill execution model proven by davidcanar/vllm-strix-halo (278-294 tok/s GLM-5.3-Flash prefill on the same 2x Strix Halo TP=2 pair over Thunderbolt) into gufo's glm5_next kernel families, reaching >= 250 tok/s serving-level (HTTP through the pair) prefill while preserving the correctness contracts: chunked-vs-tokenwise byte identity, CPU-oracle RMS caps, cross-rank hash equality, and double-precision indexer top-k. The F32-family double-accumulation contract may be relaxed to float accumulation ONLY with measured evidence it is the binding constraint, both kernel twins switched together, re-derived/verified oracle caps, and reviewer signoff; no other contract is relaxable.
+
+**Verdict:** PASS
