+- Phase 2 (Expert grouped-GEMM weight-stationary rewrite): Fix round complete. Landed the phase deliverable: BatchExpertGroupedWsKernel<Bucket,StageB,Warps,Rows> (the A-family weight-stationary template, Sub16+Vec only) in kernels_batch.hip.cpp with a three-regime launcher dispatch in BatchExpertQ8KGrouped — prefill n≥64 runs <32,16,32,1> (82 VGPRs/16 waves, weight re-read ⌈bucket/32⌉≈1.13× vs the generic tile's ≈2×), decode n<64 runs <16,8,16,2> (17.5 KiB LDS, n=1 launches 25-40% faster), and Q8_0/odd geometry keeps the original generic kernel verbatim; grid math and the executor are untouched, and prof.py's stage map gained the new kernel name. Fixed the two bench harness bugs the reviewers found (tokenwise loop now scatters global pair indices; full-N routing re-run before every chunked launch), retracted the false 'latent V0 anomaly' — V0 and all variants are chunked-vs-tokenwise identical in 160/160 checks at N∈{96,128,384,513,1024}×4 shapes×2 routings, re-verified on an -O2 rebuild matching production codegen. Ran the full gate suite on the integrated tree: executor oracle PASS at the unchanged 7.484e-07 (bit-identical twins), exec-513 ×3 / exec-2052 / exec-2049 byte-identical (exercising cross-regime dispatch), dsa_ops/batch_select/kda/mhc PASS, decode guard 16.60 ms/token (inside 16.6-16.9), check-format PASS 557 files. Measured before/after with matched binaries on a quiet GPU (production parked for the A/B after the probe OOM-killed it, then restored): slice 834.1-836.5→841.0 tok/s @512 and 713.7→716.2 @4096; pair probe 87.9/86.4→89.2/88.9 tok/s (disjoint bands, +2.2%); expert family per 512-chunk 81.6→78.8 ms (rocprofv3, Ws kernel confirmed dispatching). Wrote notes/experts-ws-250.md with the full variant sweep table (shapes, VGPR/waves, LDS, timings, bit-identity), the rejected Y-family, the winner + dispatch, the re-read-factor roofline table (1.13 ≤ 2), the explicit unit interpretation of the 3479 ms mandate, and the measured blocking-ceiling derivation: the family is register/occupancy-bound (same-traffic VGPR pairs separate 40%; 2× x-mandate costs only +9%; every rpb-raising shape spills or loses occupancy), the x-restaging term (4.3 GB/call at 1024-wide TP2 gate vs 0.68 GB weights-once) is register-capped, and the 3.86× cut is unreachable by tile restructuring within {256 VGPR, 64 KiB LDS, twin bit-identity} — the ceiling branch of criterion 1.
