+## The phase-7 bounded iteration: split-launch absorbed sparse MLA
+
+Target picked from the phase-5/6 census: after phases 2–4 the two largest
+mover families were at measured ceilings, leaving **sparse MLA attention**
+(4482.3 ms per 4096-token chunk per rank, 13.1 % of kernel time — the
+largest *depth-scaling* residual and the identified-but-untested lever of
+the prior campaign's phase 4: "splitting the fused kernel into
+score/softmax and gather/epilogue launches … a split changes no numerics").
+
+Change (`kernels_batch.hip.cpp`, one family): the fused
+`BatchMlaAttentionTiledKernel` becomes two launches —
+`BatchMlaScoreTiledKernel<8>` (score dots + softmax, probabilities left in
+the `probs` global stripe exactly as before) and
+`BatchMlaGatherTiledKernel<8>` (weighted gather + v_b epilogue, verbatim
+loops). The fused kernel's 112-VGPR register set (score + gather/epilogue
+state live together, 512-thread blocks) capped residency at one block per
+CU; each half's smaller live set doubles the achievable residency. Inside
+the score kernel the softmax now evaluates the exponential terms
+**cooperatively into shared memory once** (512-wide instead of serially on
+the denominator thread) and reuses them for the probability writes — the
+fused kernel evaluated every `exp(double)` twice (serially in the chain and
+again in the parallel pass). The denominator is still the reference's
+serial double sum **in selection order over those exact precomputed
+terms**: summed values and addition order unchanged ⇒ bit-identical
+denominator, bit-identical probabilities, ~2× fewer double-exp evaluations
+and a ~an-order-of-magnitude shorter serial chain (count f64 adds instead
+of count dependent double-exp calls). Shared cost: sel_stride+H doubles ≈
+16.5 KiB dynamic LDS.
