@@ -0,0 +1,171 @@
+# GLM-5.3-Flash TP2 prefill 250 tok/s — phase 4: MLA prefill multi-query tiling (2026-10-10)
+
+Targets: `BatchMlaAttentionKernel` (14.7% of post-phase-3 slice kernel time,
+123.3 ms per 512-token chunk at bench depth) and `BatchMlaAbsorbKernel`
+(28.1 ms per chunk). Both were latency-bound at ~0.5–0.6 TB/s effective on
+their L2 streams with ~24 VGPRs — every (token, head) block re-fetched its
+whole operand set.
+
+All numbers: `gpu-test` build, model
+`/root/models/glm53-flash/GLM-5.3-Flash-Q4_K_XL-00001-of-00005.gguf`,
+`glm5_next_prefill_bench --layers 4 --random-tokens <N> 1 --repeat 2`
+(BEST of two passes; noise ~±1%). Slice = layers 0–2 KDA + layer 3 DSA/MoE.
+
+## Design: what tiles and what it amortizes
+
+Two new kernels in `kernels_batch.hip.cpp`, dispatched by the existing
+launchers (legacy kernels kept as the geometry fallback):
+
+- **`BatchMlaAttentionTiledKernel<H>`** — one block covers `kMlaHeads=8`
+  query heads of a `kMlaTileTokens=4`-wide token tile, 512 threads
+  (= kv_lora). Phases per token: score dots (one warp per selected latent,
+  the latent row staged in 16 lane registers **shared by all 8 heads**),
+  softmax, weighted gather (thread per lora element, the four unrolled
+  latent rows **shared by all 8 heads'** 4-interleaved-accumulator sets),
+  then a v_b epilogue that stages each panel row once and dots it against
+  **every token of the tile**.
+- **`BatchMlaAbsorbTiledKernel`** — one block per head per
+  `kMlaAbsorbTokens=8` token tile; each k_b row staged in 8 lane registers
+  feeds all 8 tokens.
+
+Amortization per 512-chunk at bench depth (avg selection ~257, 64 heads):
+latent rows in scores+gather 69 GB → **8.6 GB** (÷8), k_b panel 16.8 GB →
+2.1 GB (÷8), v_b panel 16 GB → 4 GB (÷4). Beyond traffic, each shared load
+set now feeds 8× the independent FMAs — memory-level parallelism per warp,
+which is what a latency-bound kernel actually needs.
+
+## Numerics decision: bit-identity PRESERVED (measured max|diff| = 0)
+
+Per (token, head) every accumulated value matches the legacy kernel
+bit-for-bit; only load sharing changes:
+
+- lane partials walk the reduction dimension in the same ascending
+  lane-strided order, then the same 5-step `__shfl_xor` butterfly (score
+  dots, absorb dots, v_b epilogue). The staged row registers carry identical
+  values; multiplication operand order is unchanged.
+- Softmax: the max is now computed in parallel (per-warp running max +
+  fixed-order combine) instead of serially by thread 0 — **exact** for the
+  finite scores this family produces (max is associative/commutative; NaN
+  semantics would differ but NaN scores would fail every oracle gate
+  anyway). The **denominator stays a serial double sum in selection order**
+  per head — one chain per head, the 8 chains of a block running in
+  parallel — and the exponential expression
+  `float(exp(double(s − max)) / denom)` is the reference's verbatim.
+  The `#pragma unroll 4` on the serial chain only hoists loads; the add
+  chain is sequential (reassociation is what would change bits, and no
+  fast-math is enabled; the TU already builds `-ffp-contract=on`).
+- The gather keeps the 4-interleaved-accumulator structure, the tail loop,
+  and the `((acc0+acc1)+(acc2+acc3))` combine per head; the probs scratch
+  lives in the same `probs` stripe the legacy kernel writes (scores are
+  staged there, then overwritten in place with the probabilities).
+- Both chunked and tokenwise paths dispatch the identical tiled kernels
+  (`tokens=1` runs one live slot of the same tile guarded by
+  `t_base + ts < tokens`, and the token loops are runtime-count loops —
+  no unrolled token slots, so the phase-3 FP-contraction slot hazard cannot
+  reappear).
+
+Measured: exec-513 ×3 and exec-2052 logits + persistent state
+**byte-identical (max|diff| = 0)**; executor 5-token oracle rel_rms
+**7.484e-07** (cap 2e-4; identical to the phase-3 value); dsa oracle checks
+`mla q_abs` and `mla latent` against CPU fixtures at n=1 within 5e-5.
+
+## Variant sweep (512-token bench, tok/s)
+
+| Variant | tok/s | kernel ms/chunk (rocprofv3) |
+| --- | ---: | ---: |
+| V0 phase-3 tree (legacy kernels) | 605.7–609.9 | attention 123.3, absorb 28.1 |
+| A1: absorb T=8 only | — | absorb 6.5 (**4.4×**) |
+| **M1: H=8, T_attn=4, T_abs=8 (WINNER)** | **713.5 / 712.8 / 713.4** | **attention 23.0 (5.35×), absorb 6.5** |
+| M2: H=8, T_attn=1 | 709.7 | — |
+| M3: H=8, T_attn=2 | 711.4 | — |
+| M4: H=8, T_attn=8 | 713.1 | — |
+| M5: H=4, T_attn=4 | 705.5 | — |
+| M6: H=16, T_attn=4 | 711.7 | attention 23.1, 168 VGPRs — ties H=8 |
+| M7: H=8, T_attn=4, T_abs=16 | 712.5 | — |
+| M8: H=8, T_attn=4, T_abs=4 | 711.5 | — |
+
+Readings: the T axis (v_b/k_b reuse) is flat at bench depth — the panels
+are a minor stream next to the latents; the H axis saturates between 4 and
+8 (H=16 halves the latent stream again with no time change — the kernel is
+no longer latent-stream-bound). H=8 chosen (H=16 adds 56 VGPRs for nothing;
+H=4 leaves ~1% on the table).
+
+## Rejected follow-ups (measured, kept out of the tree)
+
+- **Compile-time dims** (`sel_stride`/`kv_lora`/`v_head` as constexpr +
+  immediate offsets, flat A3 element loop): 713.5 → 675.4 tok/s, VGPRs
+  112 → 192, attention 23.0 → 63.9 ms. The addressing-mode change made
+  hipClang keep far more live address state; reverted verbatim to the
+  runtime-argument form.
+- **`__launch_bounds__(512, 2)`**: ignored by the compiler (still 112
+  VGPRs, 23.0 ms) — 2×512 threads at 112 VGPRs cannot fit the register
+  file, and the compiler preferred not to spill.
+- ** LDS-staged q_abs / sorted selections**: not attempted — instruction
+  counts say the remaining floor is the per-(token,head) FMA+butterfly+exp
+  volume, not operand fetch; sorting would break the gather's locked
+  accumulation order.
+
+Remaining floor analysis: attention at H=8 is ~23 ms/chunk at bench depth
+(~77 G warp-instructions/chunk at ~10 cycles/instr issue slots — still
+latency-dominated, now on the qa loads / butterflies / serial double
+denominators rather than the latent stream). The next structural lever
+would be splitting the fused kernel into score/softmax and gather/epilogue
+launches to cut VGPRs below the 2-block occupancy threshold — left for a
+later phase; the phases already communicate through global memory
+(`probs`, `weighted`), so a split changes no numerics.
+
+## Before/after (same binaries protocol, phase-start vs final tree)
+
+| Measurement | before | after | Δ |
+| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |
+| Slice 512-token bench | 605.7–609.9 tok/s | 712.8–713.5 tok/s | **+17.0%** |
+| Slice 4096-token bench (phase-3 reference 371.8) | — | 619.0–620.7 tok/s | **+66.9%** |
+| TP2 rank-0 slice 512-token bench (`--tp-rank 0`) | 1027.6 tok/s | 1156.5 tok/s | **+12.5%** |
+| MLA attention per 512-chunk, bench depth | 123.3 ms | 23.0 ms | **5.35×** |
+| MLA attention deepest 4096-run chunk (full ~2051 selection) | 832–845 ms (phase-1 series) | 138.9 ms | **6.0×** |
+| MLA attention avg per chunk over 4096 run | 633.5 ms (phase-1 series) | 105.6 ms | **6.0×** |
+| MLA absorb per 512-chunk | 28.1 ms | 6.5 ms | **4.4×** |
+| Decode guard (tokenwise avg, `--timing`) | 16.61–16.65 ms/tok | 16.62 ms/tok | unchanged |
+
+The 4096-run chunk series shows depth scaling clearly (phase-1 legacy
+series: 123 → 326 → 530 → 736 → 832 → 833 → 843 → 845 ms; tiled series:
+22.9 → 55.6 → 89 → 122 → ~139 ms as the selection count grows to ~2051) —
+the gap at full depth is the H-amortization working where the selection set
+is largest. Deep prefill (the serving regime the goal targets) gains the
+most.
+
+## Gates on the final tree (all PASS)
+
+| Gate | Result | Detail |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `glm5_next_executor_test` (5-token oracle) | **PASS** | worst logits rel_rms 7.484e-07, top-1 matched, reset replay exact |
+| `glm5_next_executor_test --random-tokens 513 1 --skip-oracle` ×3 | **PASS** | logits + persistent state byte-identical, max\|diff\| = 0 |
+| `glm5_next_executor_test --random-tokens 2052 1 --skip-oracle` | **PASS** | byte-identical, max\|diff\| = 0 |
+| `glm5_next_dsa_ops_test` | **PASS** | full four-layer slice on real weights; exercises the tiled kernels at n=1 (`mla q_abs`/`mla latent` oracle within 5e-5) |
+| `glm5_next_kda_ops_test` | **PASS** | worst kda rel rms 2.291e-07 (unchanged family) |
+| `glm5_next_mhc_ops_test` | **PASS** | worst mhc \|d\| 2.384e-07 |
+| `glm5_next_batch_select_test` | **PASS** | tiled batch pool selector contract |
+| `tools/ci/check-format.py` | **PASS** | after sanctioned `--fix` of my edited file |
+| production `/ready` | 200 | before, during and after the phase |
+
+Changes confined to `src/models/glm5_next/kernels/rocm/kernels_batch.hip.cpp`
+(two tiled kernels + launcher dispatch + tile constants) and
+`tools/prof/prof.py` (stage map entries for the new kernel names, so the
+`attention: absorb` / `attention: sparse mla` stages keep their meaning).
+Profile DBs: `/tmp/opencode/p4/prof/{base,h8t4,h16t4,constdims,constdims2,
+lb2,final4k}/prof_results.db`.
+
+## Next-phase pointers
+
+- Slice kernel-time split after this phase (per 512-chunk at bench depth,
+  final4k averaged): quant tiled ~280 ms (33.7%), F32 tiled ~158.3 ms
+  (19.1%), KDA recurrence ~112.3 ms (13.5%), **MLA attention ~105.6 ms
+  (12.7%, down from 14.7% but 6× cheaper)**, experts ~81.4 ms (9.8%),
+  indexer scores ~25.9 ms.
+- The pair path's remaining prefill cost is now dominated by the quant/F32
+  projections, the KDA serial scan and transport; the MLA family is a
+  minor slice for the first time.
+- If MLA attention is revisited: the floor is per-(token,head)
+  instruction volume + occupancy (112 VGPRs, 1 block/CU); a score/gather
+  kernel split is the identified (untested) lever. Compile-time dims and
+  `__launch_bounds__` are measured dead ends on this toolchain.
