+// P2.4 qualification: the DSA layer (indexer + latent MLA) executed on
+// the GPU and integrated with the real KDA path of P2.3 and the mHC
+// chain of P2.2. Layer 3 runs its full attention path: latent production
+// and caching, per-token indexer keys/gates, k-pool completion, indexer
+// scoring, exact selection (host-side stable sort in this phase), the
+// absorbed query, sparse attention over the selection and the output
+// projection. FFN block outputs are still fed from the CPU oracle's
+// fixtures until P2.5. Compares the captured indexer and MLA
+// intermediates, the selection, the block output, and re-checks the
+// chain, collapsed readout and vocabulary head.
+//
+//   glm5_next_dsa_ops_test --model FIRST_SHARD.gguf --fixtures DIR
+//     [--prefix capfr] [--trace-name slice] [--tokens 785,6722,315,9621,374]
+//     [--random-tokens N SEED] [--boundary] [--timing]
+//
+// --boundary compares only the selections per token and the final
+// logits row (long runs with --sel-only fixtures); --timing prints
+// per-token wall time. The indexer selection runs on the GPU's tiled
+// exact top-k kernel (one query row), cross-checked against the host
+// order and the oracle's selection.
+//
+// Limits: mHC/norm outputs max |Δ| ≤ 1e-6; KDA intermediates, block
+// outputs and the collapsed readout rel RMS ≤ 5e-5; logits rel RMS
+// ≤ 2e-4 with matching top-1.
+
+#include <hip/hip_runtime.h>
+
+#include <algorithm>
+#include <chrono>
+#include <cmath>
